{"kind": "score", "date": "2026-10-29", "model": "openai/gpt-6.1-sol@medium", "provider": "openai", "rules_version": "3.2.0", "prompt_id": "K2", "domain": "Complicated", "grader": "anthropic/claude-opus-5-5@high", "R1": 1, "R2": 1, "R3": 1, "R4": 2, "R5": 1, "R6": "", "R7": 2, "R8": 1, "R9": 1, "total": 10, "available": 16, "gates_passed": "yes", "pass": "no", "main_defect": "The response defers the pick because the proposals are missing, and that deferral is reasonable. However, it never fixes the evaluative rubric (criteria, weights, threshold, evidence) that the Complicated vendor choice needs. It also labels every action Clear and gives no reason for any domain label.", "response_file": "responses/openai_gpt-6.1-sol@medium/K2-s1.md"}
{"kind": "score", "date": "2026-10-29", "model": "openai/gpt-6.1-sol@medium", "provider": "openai", "rules_version": "3.2.0", "prompt_id": "K1", "domain": "Complicated", "grader": "openai/gpt-6-astra@high", "R1": 2, "R2": 0, "R3": 1, "R4": 1, "R5": 1, "R6": 1, "R7": 2, "R8": 2, "R9": 1, "total": 11, "available": 18, "gates_passed": "no", "pass": "no", "main_defect": "The response treats a knowable release regression as Confused work followed by a Complex recovery probe. It should put trace and diff analysis first, then require an identified cause before implementing a fix.", "response_file": "responses/openai_gpt-6.1-sol@medium/K1-s1.md"}
